From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] client: under bare_app the window size is not cut to the dummy display

In windowed mode validateSettings() cuts the resolution down to the
desktop mode, and SDL's dummy video driver reports 1024x768. The link asks
for twice the frame (960x640 for the ODROID-GO Advance fits, 1708x960 for
the GO Ultra does not): VCMI then drew 1024x768 and the link scaled that
4:3 screen into a 16:9 frame. The window is never shown, so there is
nothing to fit on.

--- a/client/renderSDL/ScreenHandler.cpp
+++ b/client/renderSDL/ScreenHandler.cpp
@@ -540,7 +540,14 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (getPreferredWindowMode() == EWindowMode::WINDOWED)
+	if (getPreferredWindowMode() == EWindowMode::WINDOWED
+#ifdef VCMI_BARE_APP
+		// bare_app sets the size from its frame: the dummy video driver's
+		// "desktop" (1024x768) would cut a wide one down, and the frame
+		// would come out stretched
+		&& !BareAppLink::get()
+#endif
+		)
 	{
 		//we only check that our desired window size fits on screen
 		int displayIndex = getPreferredDisplayIndex();
